Title: BLUE CRAYON
Credit: Version A — "Look"
Draft: Short cut · 13 October 2026
Notes: Running time 0:56 · Two words, said twice

FADE IN:

EXT. STREET - DUSK

Rain. Under a dripping awning, beside the bins, a small battered ROBOT hugs its knees. Sage-mint paint, rust, a dent in its egg-shaped head. Two tiny glowing eyes behind a dark visor.

It trembles.

A pair of small red sneakers stops in front of it.

THE BOY (5, curly black hair, mustard hoodie two sizes too big) crouches. Holds out his open palm.

The Robot hesitates. Then rests one fingertip in it.

Its eyes curve up into two glowing arcs.

INT. APARTMENT - NIGHT

The Boy pushes the front door open, the dripping Robot holding his hand.

PAPA (30s, short black beard, work shirt) looks up from his phone. Sees the Robot. He points at the door.

The Boy plants himself in front of the Robot. Arms spread wide. Chin trembling.

Papa holds his stare. Turns away.

INT. LIVING ROOM - DRAWING CORNER - NIGHT

Lamplight. The Robot pinches a blue crayon. It slips. Slips again.

The Boy giggles. Tears a strip of tape and tapes the crayon to the Robot's finger.

RRRIP.

.MONTAGE

MUSIC: four notes on a piano.

- Two heads bent over one sheet of paper.
- Drawings go up on the wall. The wall fills.
- Boy and Robot asleep on a pile of drawings.

INT. KITCHEN - EVENING

Papa at the table, on his phone.

The Boy runs in, holding up a drawing.

BOY
Papa, look!

Papa doesn't look up.

The Boy's arm slowly lowers. Behind him, the Robot watches.

INT. BOY'S BEDROOM - DAY

Grey rain light. The Boy in bed, flushed, small under the blanket. A drawing pad on his knees. He colours a sun, slowly.

The Robot sits beside the bed, watching him.

The Boy's eyes close. The yellow crayon rolls from his fingers, off the blanket, onto the floor.

!SAME FRAME.

The bed is empty. Neatly made.

The Robot hasn't moved. In its lap, the drawing.

INT. BOY'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Dark. Papa sits on the floor against the little bed. Black suit, tie pulled loose. He stares at nothing.

The Robot crosses to him. Holds out the drawing.

Papa doesn't look.

The Robot waits.

The glow of its eyes falls on the paper. He looks.

!INSERT - THE DRAWING

Crayon on paper. A tall stick man: PAPA, the first P backwards. A small boy: ME. A little round robot with big eyes. All three holding hands under a yellow sun, half coloured in.

!BACK TO SCENE

BOY (V.O.)
(far away)
Papa... look.

Papa's jaw clamps. Holds.

It breaks. He pulls the Robot into his chest and sobs.

!OVER PAPA'S SHOULDER

The Robot, chin on his shoulder. Arms at its sides. The drawing hangs from its taped hand.

Its eyes stay wide. Still. Fixed on the empty bed.

MUSIC: the four notes. Only three play.

> CUT TO BLACK.

>BLUE CRAYON<

>THE END<
